-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- `trait Error for` a type of another module: the help says how the
-- type is shown, not to write an impl only its own module can write.
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: trait 'Error' is not declared
-- stderr-contains: help: an error is shown as any value is: `io.IoError` is shown (by `{e}`, and as the error of main) by the Display it has
-- stderr-not-contains: write `trait Display
import io
trait Error for io.IoError { fn message(self) -> String { "b" } }
fn main() { println(1) }
